<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Krtsanisi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Krtsanisi was fought on 11 September 1795 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tbilisi</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> army of Agha Mohammad Khan and the much smaller Georgian force of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erekle-ii">Erekle II</a> of Kartli-Kakheti. Left without the Russian help promised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-georgievsk">Treaty of Georgievsk</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> were defeated, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> sacked and burned Tbilisi. The disaster hastened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>'s annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1801.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-krtsanisi.jpg" alt="Battle of Krtsanisi" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valerian Sidamon-Eristavi (1889–1943) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valerian_Sidamon-Eristavi_11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
